  the point of the table: alpha is the SMALL real part of an eigenvalue
  whose imaginary part is 324x larger, so a lag that
  perturbs the Jacobian by O(w0/w_c) can perturb alpha by O(Q w0/w_c).
  Q = w0/(2 alpha) = 162.0
